ek and Latin writers refer to the people as the Gangaridai ( variant Gandaridai) . The Sanskrit equivalent of the term is difficult to determine. Classical scholars take the word to mean "the people of the Ganges region."'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 844, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 734})
