ies of early Rome, and in particular in early Roman religion. […] Modern research has produced abundant evidence for direct Greek influence on early Roman religion.”  “As Rome expanded by treaty and conquest during the Monarchy and early Republic, it incorporated new citizens from added territories by creating new tribes of voters. At the same time, the new citizens’ gods were incorporated into the divine community, whose public cults constituted the state religion.”  “Roman religion was an amalgam of different traditions from at least as far back as we can hope to go. Leaving aside its mythical prehistory, Roman religion was always already multicultural.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 933, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 829})
